#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:628
msgid "``browser``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:628
msgid ""
"A launched headless ``chromium`` browser, shared for the duration of the "
"test session and closed on teardown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:631
msgid "``goto``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:631
msgid ""
"A factory that opens a built page at a given viewport width, defaulting to "
":bash:`index.html` e.g., :python:`page = goto(390)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:634
msgid ""
"The factory waits for the theme chrome to **settle** before handing the page"
" back, and closes every page that it opened on teardown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:640
msgid ""
"Both themes inject their toggles from ``JavaScript`` *after* the page has "
"loaded, so the chrome is not final the moment the page is ready. The factory"
" therefore polls until the toggle count stops changing, rather than pausing "
"for a fixed delay - a delay tuned on a developer machine is apt to be too "
"short on a loaded CI runner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:646
msgid "``html_root``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:646
msgid ""
"The root directory of the documentation build, :bash:`docs/_build/html`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:648
msgid "``api_page``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:648
msgid "The path of a built API reference page, relative to ``html_root``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:650
msgid ""
"Such a page carries a secondary *On this page* sidebar with enough entries "
"to be worth revealing, which the landing page does not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:653
msgid "``require``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:653
msgid ""
"A guard for a prerequisite that only a unit test itself can detect, such as "
"the gallery carousel, which **skips** or, under ``--browser-strict``, "
"**fails** e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:657
