msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:665
msgid "Helpers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:669
msgid ":bash:`tests/docs/_theme.py`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:671
msgid ""
"The :bash:`tests/docs/_theme.py` module provides the helpers that browser "
"unit tests use to interrogate the theme chrome, such as "
":python:`click_visible` to activate a toggle, :python:`dialog` to report the"
" state of a sidebar dialog, and :python:`sidebar_offset` to distinguish a "
"sidebar that collapses in place from one that opens as a dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:677
msgid ""
"Both themes render a **duplicate** of each toggle and hide one of them, so "
"\"the button\" is ambiguous - the helpers consistently act upon the one that"
" a reader can actually see."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:684
msgid ""
"The ``sphinx-design`` :python:`sd-stretched-link` class covers its card "
"through an :python:`::after` overlay, so the bounding rectangle of the "
"anchor itself is no more than its text. Click coverage must therefore be "
"verified by hit-testing with :python:`document.elementFromPoint`, and "
"**not** by comparing rectangles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../geovista/docs/src/developer/testing.rst:689
msgid ""
"A carousel also deliberately hangs its cards past its own clipping edge, so "
"only those cards lying wholly inside the clipping rectangle can be hit-"
"tested - assert that at least one card qualifies, otherwise the unit test "
"passes vacuously."
msgstr ""

